  "text": {
    "tagline": "The keyboard floor, 1985.",
    "blurb": "Walk the 1985 keyboard floor again: big polyphonic brass and strings, fat monophonic basses and leads, glassy FM pianos and clavs, and choirs from the vocoder corner. {count} presets for SNDWAVE2000 and BASILISK SYNTH.",
    "intro": [
      "Welcome to the Polysynth Showroom, the in-store demo disc of the Neon Keys keyboard department. Every preset recalls a sound from the great showroom floor of the mid-eighties: polyphonic pads and brass, monophonic basses and leads, FM pianos and clavs, vocoder choirs and string machines.",
      "No keyboard was harmed, and none is named: our keyboard specialists rebuilt every sound for the Sound Recorder synthesizer."
    ],
    "maker_note": [
      "Come down to any Neon Keys store, play the floor models, and ask for the Showroom disc at the counter.",
      "The Neon Keys Keyboard Department"
    ],
    "install": [
      "Insert the disc. In the Library tab it appears as POLYSHOW85.",
      "Open a folder and double-click a preset to load it.",
      "The demo guide is POLYSHOW.PDF; the sound credits are in CREDITS.TXT."
    ],
